transaction (a merge of main, a resume) is patched from the datoms the two values differ by. A change of the pattern, or one that moves where an entity is held (a new run reaching the task, the holder leaving its window), builds the record anew, as a fresh build places it, and shares back every subtree it did not change (the same objects): that patch costs the record, once a run."], :functions [["seon.docs/resolve-ref 93%: Var sym as its citation's depth shows it (docs/references.md#the-delimiter-picks-the-depth):\n  :summary its arglists and its doc's first sentence, :doc its arglists, doc and contract,\n  :code its source (from the db), whole: the printer cuts it where it is shown, with the form\n  that reads its rest; at :doc a var with no doc shows its source. A name that resolves to\n  nothing says so. A var the db holds is read from its facts (its doc, its contract, its\n  recorded source and the arglists it declares), so what it shows changes as the db does; a\n  library var the db does not hold, from the process's var meta, which its build fixes." [:seon.print/prose :seon.ref/depth :var/contract :var/doc :var/name]] ["seon.context/world 73%: What changed for agent entity a between two commits of its branch on db (the ones a turn's\n  request and the one before it were made on), as data: {:page {key hiccup}, each part of its page whose hiccup changed (nil for one\n  that went), :ctx {path [old new]}, seon.ctx/diff of its record advanced across them, every path that\n  changed}, the empty ones left out; in the diff the agent's own records, which its conversation\n  already shows, are told by what reads them: an eval by its handle, a turn by its id; with no c0, the page whole,\n  {:page page}.\n  Printed whole as one user message: the page and each change told once." [:seon.agent/branch :seon.eval/id :seon.model/message :seon.turn/id]] ["seon.program/meaning 68%: What a definition says of itself that text describing it relies on, so what a wiki section\n  citing it goes stale on (seon.problems/stale-sections) and an eval that changes it shows\n  (meaning-changes): its contract and its docstring, the facts def-tx asserts and retracts\n  (DECISIONS Dogfood rulings; the contract carries the arity)." [:var/contract :var/doc]] ["seon.program/reach-step 59%: Graph g after the forms removed (ids) and the rows added (reach-rows', live on db): each form's neighbours recomputed only where its edges can have changed (an added form; a form referring to, naming in a test's namespace (:quoted), or defining the methods, extensions or contract of, a var a changed form defines), and the components of the changed forms and of every form reaching them re-folded (components over those alone, the rest kept)." [:seon.config.source/binary-vars :seon.config.source/process-vars :var/contract :var/kind :var/name]] ["seon.problems/stale-sections 57%: Each section whose text cites a var whose contract or docstring changed since the section was last written or reviewed, as a :stale-section row naming what changed (:changed), what it was as of then (:was) and what it is (:now): the var's facts (seon.program/meaning) as of the transaction that wrote the section's :seon.section/read (seon.docs/load-tx) or its :seon.section/reviewed (my.docs/reviewed!), read from history, against now." [:seon.problems/row :seon.section/address :seon.section/baseline-unread :seon.section/read :seon.section/reviewed :var/contract :var/doc :var/name]]], :schemas [[:seon.db/var-fact "61%"]]}}
